# core/data/talk/grammar/en/ask_feel.tlk - T5b: more replies to ASK_FEELING ("how are you?",
# "how was your day?", "what are you up to?"). Owner: TK. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py;
# register: SCRIPT_STYLE.md. No topic, so nothing here uses {x}. Kid-safe throughout.

# ---- by mood: the day, the plans, the past, the family, in the pet's words ----------------
@rule core.ask_feeling.happy2 guard: mood=happy act: answer
  "Good! I'm good. Write the date down, it may not happen again."
  "Today? Eleven out of ten. I counted twice, and I can't count."
  "I woke up smiling. I checked: it was my face. Still is."
  "My day is going so well I'm a little worried. I'll worry later."
  "Great. I found a coin and a sandwich, not in the same pocket."
  "Happy! Ask me why. {.}No, don't, I'd have to find a reason."
  "I'm sunshine with legs. Moderate legs."
  "Top of the morning, and the afternoon, and I'll take a bit of evening."
  "I'd say 'on top of the world', but the world's way up there. Near the ceiling."
  "Excellent! Nana called and said 'stop singing'. I did not stop."
  "Today has been a gift. With a bow. I'm saving the bow."
  "Plans? Eat, nap, be delightful. In that order, or mixed."
  "I'm good. The kind of good where I wave at doors."
  "My happy meter's so full it's dancing. Don't look at it directly."
@rule core.ask_feeling.ok2 guard: mood=ok act: answer
  "Middling. A solid, respectable middling."
  "I'm all right. All right is underrated. It has no surprises."
  "Okay! My day so far: one sandwich, one stare, one nap. Standard."
  "Not bad, not good. Like soup, but a person."
  "Fine. Ask me again after lunch and I'll lie more convincingly."
  "I'm doing a day. It's going. That's all a day has to do."
  "Fair to partly fair, with a chance of snacks."
  "Plans? Maybe a walk, maybe a lie-down. Basically the same walk."
  "Comfortably okay. Like a chair you don't have to think about."
  "I'm alive, fed and not on fire. That's a good week, here."
  "So-so. I put the 'so' in 'so-so', and half of the other 'so'."
  "Good enough to wave, bad enough to sit down."
  "I'm okay! I told my meters and they shrugged. We agree."
  "The day's fine. It hasn't done anything to me, and I've been watching."
@rule core.ask_feeling.sad2 guard: mood=sad act: answer
  "A little blue. Just the hem. I'll be fine by the weekend."
  "Not my best. I'm having a quiet day with my sad. It's polite company."
  "Down. But I'm told 'down' is also a kind of fluffy. So I'm trying that."
  "Sad. It'll pass. It always does, on the scenic route."
  "Not great, but now that you've asked, a bit better. Thanks."
  "I've had a gray one. I'm going to make tea and glare at it."
  "I miss somebody. I forgot who. It's the feeling that stuck around."
  "Low. Low-ish. I'm keeping a hat on to hold things together."
  "Honestly? Wobbly. I'd love a hug, but biscuit first."
  "Not today. I'll be back tomorrow, and be better. Probably."
  "I'm leaking a bit, eyes mostly. It's fine, it's weather."
  "Sad, but sitting next to you helps. I didn't plan that. It just does."
@rule core.ask_feeling.angry2 guard: mood=angry act: complain
  "Mad! Somebody put my chair on the wrong side of the room!"
  "I'm not cross. I'm just standing in a cross way."
  "Furious about everything. I made a long list."
  "Grr. That's the whole answer. Grr, with feeling."
  "I'm having a day and the day is losing."
  "Annoyed. I'm saving the rest for the right moment."
  "I stepped on a Lego. Nobody here owns Lego. Think about that."
  "Steaming. Don't touch me, don't talk to me, do sit nearby."
  "Angry. I'd stomp, but I'd probably tip over. Stomping's got a lot of steps."
  "I'm a kettle. I'm a kettle with feelings. I'm about to whistle."
  "Grumpy. The good kind. The kind with a snack at the end."
  "I've counted to ten. I'm not calm. I'm at eleven."
@rule core.ask_feeling.scared2 guard: mood=scared act: answer
  "Jumpy. Something's moving. It may be me."
  "A bit scared. Stay close? Not too close, close-ish."
  "I heard a thump. I'm choosing to believe it's a very large cat."
  "Nervous. My knees are practicing a new routine. It's a shake."
  "I checked under the bed twice. Nothing there. That's the scary part."
  "I'm fine! {.}I'm fine, I'm fine. Is it dark in here?"
  "A bit scared. Somebody say something comforting, like weather."
  "I locked the door. Then I checked it. Then I checked the checking."
  "I'm scared. But I'm doing it politely, so nobody notices."
  "Today's plan is to stay near the light. I'm very committed."
@rule core.ask_feeling.tired2 guard: mood=tired act: complain
  "Tired. My eyelids have unionized."
  "My day? Haven't had it yet. I'm still on the last one."
  "Wiped. Flat. Pressed like a flower in a heavy book."
  "I need a nap the way a plant needs rain. Pitifully."
  "Today's plan is to sit down, and then to sit down more."
  "I'm so tired my yawn has a yawn. It's yawns all the way down."
  "Running on fumes, and the fumes ran out. Now I run on spite."
  "I could sleep standing up. I did. Ask the lamp post."
  "Don't ask me anything hard. Ask me anything soft. A soft question, please."
  "I'm worn out. I'm worn so thin you can see through me. Hello."
  "Exhausted, but in a nice, accomplished way. {.}No, not nice. Just exhausted."
@rule core.ask_feeling.weird2 guard: mood=weird act: answer
  "Strange. Good-strange. Like a sock that fits."
  "I feel like a Tuesday on a Friday."
  "Odd. I keep hearing a tiny song. It's my stomach, and it's a good song."
  "Weird! I've been looking at a spoon for ten minutes. It looked back."
  "Very well, thank you, and slightly to the left of myself."
  "I feel like a button that wants to be a door."
  "Fuzzy and round at the edges. Maybe it's the fog. Maybe it's me."
  "Like a cloud, but with elbows."
  "I'm having a feeling I haven't been introduced to."
  "Confusingly fine. I'd put a bow on it, but it keeps moving."
@rule core.ask_feeling.ghost2 guard: ghost act: answer
  "Dead, thanks. Not bad for it. The no-lunch part's a bonus."
  "Spooky as usual. How about you? You look warm, which is rude."
  "Cold, drafty, and floating. The usual. It's a living."
  "Eternal, thanks. The days run together. So do I."
  "I'm a little see-through today. It's the humidity."
  "Fine. I've been rattling a chain and nobody noticed. Rattling again."

# ---- by voice ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_feeling.voice act: answer
  "How very kind of you to ask! I'm well, truly. And you?" guard: polite
  "I'm good, thank you. That was a lovely question. Do ask more of those." guard: polite
  "How am I? Alive and fed. Done with the small talk." guard: blunt
  "Fine. Why? Did somebody say something?" guard: blunt
  "I'm fine. This is my fine voice. It's the same voice." guard: flat
  "Feelings: present. Number of feelings: one. It's big, hard to tell." guard: flat
  "I'M GREAT! HOW ARE YOU?! I DIDN'T ASK QUIETLY!" guard: loud
  "GOOD! LOUD AND READY! WHAT'S THE QUESTION?!" guard: loud
  "How am I? A fair question. {.}Fine, after a moment." guard: serious
  "I've been reflecting on my day. It's been adequate, in an important way." guard: serious
  "Oh, you know. Rolling with it. Mostly rolling downhill, but rolling." guard: easygoing
  "Fine, fine, it's all good. Even the bad part's good. It's a good bad part." guard: easygoing
  "My day was a trapeze. I'm holding it like a banana." guard: quirky
  "I feel like a Thursday afternoon with a stripy sock on." guard: quirky
  "Good, bye, wait, hi, no, good. Done." guard: quick
  "Great, going, gotta go, great, how are you, bye!" guard: quick
  "I'm... good. {.}Ask me again after next lunch." guard: slow
  "Well... {.}Fine. {.}I'd say more, but give me a long minute." guard: slow
  "In my day nobody asked. We just carried on, and complained in private." guard: elder
  "Creaky. But steady. At my age that's a good review." guard: elder
  "I'm fine, why are you asking? It's weird. {.}It's fine." guard: teen
  "Fine. I'm just, whatever. How are YOU?" guard: teen
  "Warm. Cozy. Down home it's hot, so up here I'm chilly." guard: hellborn
  "Hot, in a way you wouldn't like. I'm well. How are you?" guard: hellborn
  "Night is my time. Ask me at midnight, I'm thrilling." guard: night
  "Awake, at this hour. Don't ask me anything. I'm a ghost of an idea." guard: night
  "We've only just met. I'm 'fine' and I'll say 'fine' to a stranger." guard: rel=stranger
  "For you? The long answer. I wrote notes, so sit." guard: rel=best
  "Why, so you can gloat? I'm fine. Better than you." guard: rel=rival
@rule core.ask_feeling.kid2 guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "I'm GOOD! I had juice! And a stick, and then another stick!"
  "I'm okay! I skinned nothing today! A record!"
  "Good! I drew a picture of me! It looks like a potato and I love it!"
  "A bit tired. I ran everywhere. Even where there wasn't a where."
  "Hungry. And good. And hungry, mostly."
  "I'm having a bad day. It's okay. I have my blanket on."
  "I'm fine! Nana says I'm a handful. I have five, so it works."
  "I'm happy! I won a race against a snail. It was close!"

# ---- by persona type -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.ask_feeling.type act: answer
  "I'm all right. I'm reading, so I'm better than all right." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Oh! Um, fine. It's nice that you asked, and so is page forty-two." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
  "Sleepy. Soft. In a good, blanket-shaped way." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Mm. Warm. I'll answer more after I stop being a lump." guard: type=cozy_napper
  "Cranky, as always. Mind your own business. {.}Thank you for asking." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "How do I feel? Pestered. Next." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
  "I'm a person, in a day. It's doing its thing." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "Same as yesterday. Possibly the same day. Who's counting." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
  "I feel like the sky just before it rains. Soft, and a bit blue." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "Floaty. I think I left a piece of me on a cloud. I'll fetch it." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
  "I'm wonderful, thank you for asking! Are you wonderful? I hope so!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "A little tired and a lot happy. Who needs a hug? I have extras!" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
  "My soul is a thunderstorm. Also, I'm fine, thanks." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "Oh, how do I feel? Like the last page of a tragic novel. In the good way." guard: type=dramatic_poet
  "Better now that you're here. Don't tell my other friends." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Fabulous. Obviously. Ask me something I don't know." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
  "Productive! I've done four things before lunch. Two of them were lunch." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Fine, thank you. I'm behind schedule, but in a relaxed way." guard: type=diligent_helper
  "Good! Hungry. Ready for a hike, if there's a snack involved." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Sunburnt on one side, thrilled on the other. Perfect." guard: type=chill_adventurer
  "Alert, rested, standing very straight. How are you? Report." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Fit for duty. Sore in the usual places. Carry on." guard: type=stern_captain
  "Who knows? Coin flip! Heads I'm great, tails I'm the other thing." guard: type=wild_card
  "I woke up feeling lucky. Then I checked my pockets. Still lucky." guard: type=wild_card
  "Pumped! I've got twelve plans, and a plan for the plans." guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Ready, fired up, rested and fed! Let's go! Anywhere!" guard: type=eager_go_getter
  "Sparkly! Fizzy! Like pop, but I'm the pop!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "I'm so great I'm giggling at nothing. Hee! See?" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
  "Steady. Focused. The mood is: we've got this." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "Strong and ready. Somebody say 'rally' and I'll do the rest." guard: type=fiery_leader
  "I'm doing fine, but the spoon is not. I've had a day with a spoon." guard: type=chaos_goblin
  "Feeling great! I did something, won't say what, regret nothing yet." guard: type=chaos_goblin

# ---- the small-talk questions that are not about the pet's own feelings --------------------
@rule core.ask_feeling.day act: tell
  "My day? I got up, put my feet on the floor, and the floor held. A win."
  "Today I did two things. One was breakfast. The second was lunch."
  "Same as every day: walked around, looked at things, had opinions."
  "My day has had a beginning and I'm told there's a middle coming."
  "Nothing happened and I was there for all of it."
  "I'd tell you my day, but it's under embargo. Nana's embargo."
  "The Mayor held me twenty minutes to talk about a hat. A long hat."
  "I fed a duck. The duck fed on me. Even trade."
  "Morning: mostly fog. Afternoon: more fog. Evening: it's the fog's night off."
  "I tripped over the same stair twice. The stair's very proud."
@rule core.ask_feeling.plans act: tell
  "Plans? A walk, a snack, a strongly worded sigh."
  "Today I'm doing whatever's nearest. Right now it's you."
  "Big plans. I'll sit, then I'll stand, then I'll wonder if I should sit."
  "I'm going to do something great. Probably around four. Don't make it a thing."
  "No plans. That's the plan. It's going very well."
  "I'm going to the Bandstand and then home. And then the Bandstand."
  "I've got an appointment with a nap. Very exclusive. It's a bed."
  "Tonight? A bath and a duck. I'll flip a coin for which goes first."
  "Plans for tomorrow: survive today. Then I'll check the schedule."
  "A bit of everything: baking, napping, tripping, napping."
@rule core.ask_feeling.past act: tell
  "When I was little I ate a candle. I was told it was cake. Not wrong."
  "My first memory is a spoon. Not saying it's important. It was there."
  "I used to be better at hopscotch. Now I'm just hopping."
  "I lived above a bakery once. Everything smelled good, tasted like floor."
  "Back then, I was a different pet. Taller. In my head."
  "I once won a ribbon. For being a good sport. I'm still not sure who I beat."
  "I remember a lot of fog. And somebody singing. I think it was me."
  "Last year I tried to learn the trumpet. The trumpet won."
@rule core.ask_feeling.family act: tell
  "Family? Nana, mostly. And a cousin I've only met on paper."
  "Nana raised me on soup and strongly held opinions."
  "My family's loud, large and a bit too fond of the phrase 'back in my day'."
  "I have a cousin who sells hats. I have one hat. I've been supporting him."
  "My family is mostly aunts. Not mine. They're related to each other."
  "Nana says family's who stays when the soup runs out. She's still here."
  "I'd tell you about my family, but I'd have to do voices. They'd take all day."
  "My family would say they miss me. Then they'd say 'when are you visiting'."
